From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brennoflavio <contato@brennoflavio.com.br>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:03:44 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] webapi: scroll modal descendants and measure nested overflow

Fix native Playwright navigation to Amazon Brazil's Subscribe & Save
address selector. The address link lives below the viewport in a fixed
modal, but scrollIntoViewIfNeeded previously returned for every fixed
descendant and otherwise scrolled only the owning window. The inner
scroller also reported only five pixels of content, clamping any manual
scroll before it could expose the link.

Walk ancestor scroll containers inside-out, recomputing target geometry
after each move. Stop window propagation at viewport-fixed boundaries,
not before scrolling the modal's contents. Skip scrollers that an
out-of-flow target escapes through its containing block. Compute deltas
in each scroller's local space, excluding its and outer transforms while
preserving transforms inside it.

Measure descendant overflow on scrollable axes without changing the
existing synthetic client-box sizing. Keep outer ranges independent of
nested scrolling, hidden/clip boundaries, and escaping positioned boxes.
Cache both flow coordinates in one preorder pass to avoid recounting
preceding sibling subtrees for every descendant. Extend the existing
inline-style parser expectations for the new clipping flags; add no
upstream tests.

Validation: Debug and ReleaseFast builds; all 1658 upstream tests pass.
The account-free fixed-modal fixture now scrolls its inner container and
accepts a normal Playwright click (published baseline times out; Chrome
control succeeds). Thirteen temporary probe cases cover scale/rotation,
inner transforms, positioned overflow stability, hidden/clip/nested
scrollers, deeply wrapped collapsed content, visible targets, relative
CDP rectangles, and a 2000-element list. Address-selector navigation
succeeds with ordinary link clicks at 1280x720 and 1920x1080 after reload;
separate CDP geometry checks agree and elementFromPoint hits the link.
No forced clicks, direct-link navigation, or account changes are needed.
One reviewer pass identified transformed deltas, escaping positioned
boxes, clipping propagation, and repeated traversal costs; all addressed.
